codeWithHeader Example from <b>1 languages</b>: <a href="../concepts/python.html">Python</a>
 print(&quot;Hello&quot;, end=&quot;!\n&quot;)
 
 # details: any parameter that hasn&#39;t been explicitly marked as positional-only
 # can be provided as a named argument

codeWithHeader Example from <b>1 languages</b>: <a href="../concepts/ruby.html">Ruby</a>
 String.new(&quot;abc&quot;, encoding: &quot;utf-8&quot;, capacity: 16)

codeWithHeader Example from <b>1 languages</b>: <a href="../concepts/scala.html">Scala</a>
 &quot;abcdef&quot;.slice(from=2, until=4)

codeWithHeader Example from <b>1 languages</b>: <a href="../concepts/kotlin.html">Kotlin</a>
 &quot;abcdef&quot;.subSequence(startIndex=2, endIndex=4)

***

* Languages *with* Named Arguments include <a href="../concepts/python.html">Python</a>, <a href="../concepts/ruby.html">Ruby</a>, <a href="../concepts/scala.html">Scala</a>, <a href="../concepts/kotlin.html">Kotlin</a>

***

* Languages *without* Named Arguments include <a href="../concepts/javascript.html">JavaScript</a>, <a href="../concepts/c.html">C</a>, <a href="../concepts/java.html">Java</a>, <a href="../concepts/cpp.html">C++</a>, <a href="../concepts/typescript.html">TypeScript</a>, <a href="../concepts/bash.html">Bash</a>, <a href="../concepts/rust.html">Rust</a>, <a href="../concepts/haskell.html">Haskell</a>

